<title>SPAIN: Small quake strikes southern Spain, no damage.</title>
<headline>Small quake strikes southern Spain, no damage.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A small earthquake struck the area round Granada in southern Spain at around 0715 GMT on Monday, but there were no reports of casualties or damage, local press and radio reported.</p>
<p>They said the quake measured 4.3 on the Richter scale, and its epicentre was in Ventas de Huelma, around 30 km from Granada.</p>
<p>The quake was reported to have lasted around 10 seconds.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
